WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.280 --> 00:00:05.800
When it comes to anomalous religions, the
SCP Foundation is no stranger to them.

00:00:05.800 --> 00:00:11.420
The weird, wild, and utterly incomprehensible
belief systems that populate the world of

00:00:11.420 --> 00:00:17.050
the anomalous might seem too crazy and dangerous
to participate in on paper, but if there’s

00:00:17.050 --> 00:00:22.180
anything that brings people together, it’s
the power of faith and belief.

00:00:22.180 --> 00:00:27.130
Take for example the Mekhanites, a massive
religious following with various sects located

00:00:27.130 --> 00:00:32.759
across the globe, united in their belief that
body-modification using technology is the

00:00:32.759 --> 00:00:38.390
pathway to worship their god, Mekhane, the
Broken God who will one day reassemble the

00:00:38.390 --> 00:00:44.690
lost parts of its body and usher the universe
into a new age of technological superiority.

00:00:44.690 --> 00:00:50.350
Or the cult-like Children of the Scarlet King,
who worship a brutal ancient entity known

00:00:50.350 --> 00:00:56.609
as the Scarlet King, who exists as a dangerous
idea, unable to be accurately described or

00:00:56.609 --> 00:01:03.499
cataloged by contemporary science, separating
the ages of modernity and antiquity, and invigorating

00:01:03.499 --> 00:01:07.869
its followers to commit horrible acts in the
name of their King.

00:01:07.869 --> 00:01:12.030
But if you’re a long time viewer of SCP
Explained, then chances are you’ve heard

00:01:12.030 --> 00:01:17.300
of the Broken God and the Scarlet King, arguably
two of the most popular anomalous religions.

00:01:17.300 --> 00:01:23.240
So today, we’re going to be talking about
one you might not have heard about – Fifthism.

00:01:23.240 --> 00:01:27.969
Fifthism is a lot more difficult to explain,
because instead of a central prevailing deity

00:01:27.969 --> 00:01:34.170
and strict belief system that unites Fifthists,
the religion is defined more by its nonsensical,

00:01:34.170 --> 00:01:39.689
illogical, and absurd state of mind that it
imposes on its followers.

00:01:39.689 --> 00:01:45.810
Fifthism is all consuming, a mindset that
is often transmitted through memetic means,

00:01:45.810 --> 00:01:50.750
such as books that contain rambling paragraphs
of surreal imagery and platitudes that are

00:01:50.750 --> 00:01:54.720
dispersed among unsuspecting populations by
Fifthists.

00:01:54.720 --> 00:02:00.079
Those who read Fifthist literature often succumb
to Fifthist beliefs themselves, losing their

00:02:00.079 --> 00:02:06.150
mind and delving into a strange world centered
around cosmic starfish and the number five,

00:02:06.150 --> 00:02:10.500
where nothing makes sense, but it doesn’t
matter, because you’ve now been enlightened,

00:02:10.500 --> 00:02:14.430
and to the Fifthist zealot, it all makes sense.

00:02:14.430 --> 00:02:19.530
The Foundation had to deal with a dangerous
piece of Fifthist literature in the past.

00:02:19.530 --> 00:02:25.840
SCP-1425, the book titled Star Signals, was
a self-help book with memetic properties that

00:02:25.840 --> 00:02:31.010
nearly consumed the mind’s of the entire
world, becoming a national best-seller, that

00:02:31.010 --> 00:02:36.099
forced the Foundation to take extreme measures
to purge it from public knowledge and destroy

00:02:36.099 --> 00:02:38.040
every remaining copy.

00:02:38.040 --> 00:02:43.870
Just listen to this excerpt from SCP-1425,
which illustrates the strange, mind-altering

00:02:43.870 --> 00:02:45.140
Fifthist doctrine.

00:02:45.140 --> 00:02:50.489
“Now imagine that the place where your desires
are made real has a name.

00:02:50.489 --> 00:02:52.989
It’s called the Fifth World.

00:02:52.989 --> 00:02:58.970
The Fifth World is the cosmos twisted around
you into the shape you will wish for.

00:02:58.970 --> 00:03:01.920
It has never been, but you can make it so.

00:03:01.920 --> 00:03:06.900
If the current world is like a tight, collared
suit, then the Fifth World is like a flowing

00:03:06.900 --> 00:03:10.269
robe that allows complete freedom of movement.

00:03:10.269 --> 00:03:14.650
You will never truly move before you move
in the Fifth World.

00:03:14.650 --> 00:03:20.130
You’ll feel like a square on a piece of
paper who was only just made about up and

00:03:20.130 --> 00:03:21.130
down.”

00:03:21.130 --> 00:03:25.950
When dealing with Fifthism, that’s the kind
of strangeness you’re guaranteed to encounter.

00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:31.380
The Foundation’s operation to get SCP-1425
under control took weeks, and didn’t work

00:03:31.380 --> 00:03:36.500
out as smoothly as they hoped, proving the
religion as a force to be reckoned with, and

00:03:36.500 --> 00:03:39.470
definitely not one to take lightly.

00:03:39.470 --> 00:03:45.170
But the story of Star Signals, SCP-1425, is
one for another day.

00:03:45.170 --> 00:03:51.810
Now that you have a crash course in Fifthism,
we can get to the real reason you’re here:

00:03:51.810 --> 00:03:54.969
SCP-2456 Dreams of a Broken World.

00:03:54.969 --> 00:03:57.069
What exactly is SCP-2456?

00:03:57.069 --> 00:04:02.760
Well, if you guessed that it’s Fifthist,
you would be correct, but considering what

00:04:02.760 --> 00:04:06.709
we know about Fifthism, that could mean anything!

00:04:06.709 --> 00:04:12.890
SCP-2456’s discovery dates back to a Foundation
operation in Eugene Orgeon, where Foundation

00:04:12.890 --> 00:04:17.769
operatives raided the hideout of individuals
belonging to the Serpent’s Hand, a para-military

00:04:17.769 --> 00:04:23.290
resistance organization unified by their belief
that the world should embrace the anomalous.

00:04:23.290 --> 00:04:27.870
The Serpent’s Hand has been heavily critical
of groups like the Global Occult Coalition

00:04:27.870 --> 00:04:33.150
and SCP Foundation, their containment, and
especially their destruction of anomalous

00:04:33.150 --> 00:04:35.020
objects and entities.

00:04:35.020 --> 00:04:40.420
In an ideal world for a member of the Hand,
anomalies co-exist with the world we know.

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:45.419
It’s an idealistic picture, but their antagonism
against the Foundation has painted a serious

00:04:45.419 --> 00:04:50.509
target on their back, subjecting them to frequent
ambushes and raids on their hideouts.

00:04:50.509 --> 00:04:56.550
And that’s exactly what happened inside
the abandoned warehouse where SCP-2456 was

00:04:56.550 --> 00:04:57.550
discovered.

00:04:57.550 --> 00:05:02.181
The Foundation sent a highly trained Mobile
Task Force, a squad named Bookworms, after

00:05:02.181 --> 00:05:09.000
one of the remaining copies of SCP-1425, the
Fifthist self-help book Star Signals, which

00:05:09.000 --> 00:05:12.300
was supposedly stowed away inside the warehouse.

00:05:12.300 --> 00:05:16.120
Upon entry, the operatives stumbled upon a
Serpent’s Hand hideout, and a firefight

00:05:16.120 --> 00:05:19.639
between Hand members and Foundation operatives
ensued.

00:05:19.639 --> 00:05:24.300
The Task Force suffered minor casualties,
but they managed to secure a hold over the

00:05:24.300 --> 00:05:26.310
warehouse after a brief struggle.

00:05:26.310 --> 00:05:31.419
Inside, they not only found the copy of Star
Signals, but several other anomalous artifacts

00:05:31.419 --> 00:05:34.350
that the Hand was using to further its goals.

00:05:34.350 --> 00:05:39.370
During the inventory, another curious object
was found, a wooden crate with a label that

00:05:39.370 --> 00:05:43.600
read ‘FIFTH CYCLE OF THE MIND’ stamped
onto its side.

00:05:43.600 --> 00:05:48.539
When opened, the Foundation uncovered dozens
more copies of Star Signals, as well as numerous

00:05:48.539 --> 00:05:53.170
other Fifthist texts, and a weathered note
signed by an unknown individual that read:

00:05:53.170 --> 00:05:57.699
“George, this is our latest catch; please
burn these as soon as you can at your discretion.

00:05:57.699 --> 00:05:59.690
Don't let the idiots find this.”

00:05:59.690 --> 00:06:04.370
At the very bottom of the crate, several manuscripts
were discovered that contained information

00:06:04.370 --> 00:06:10.010
about a then-unknown Fifthist anomaly involving
a strange variation of the belief system,

00:06:10.010 --> 00:06:12.780
which the Foundation immediately began researching.

00:06:12.780 --> 00:06:17.840
The manuscripts pointed towards the existence
of an abstract theology that has existed for

00:06:17.840 --> 00:06:23.039
centuries, that, when preached by its believers,
transmits a memetic virus.

00:06:23.039 --> 00:06:28.760
This religion is varying in characteristics,
but is distinguishable by several qualities,

00:06:28.760 --> 00:06:33.199
such as starting out as a variation of an
existing theology, making frequent use of

00:06:33.199 --> 00:06:37.460
the number five in its written doctrine, and
revolving around godhead figures that are

00:06:37.460 --> 00:06:42.470
synonymous with the sun, who are believed
to bring about a future apocalypse.

00:06:42.470 --> 00:06:47.380
On top of those, written works make mention
of a nonexistent sea, frequent references

00:06:47.380 --> 00:06:52.389
to celestial objects, the appearance of hands
as a religious symbol, and the belief that

00:06:52.389 --> 00:06:56.199
the sun has great mathematical significance
and importance.

00:06:56.199 --> 00:07:01.020
If all of that sounds confusing to you, congratulations,
you’re immune to Fifthism.

00:07:01.020 --> 00:07:07.020
If it sounds appealing, well, you might just
be affected by SCP-2456.

00:07:07.020 --> 00:07:13.759
SCP-2456 is a memetic parasite, transmitted
from one person to another by being exposed

00:07:13.759 --> 00:07:20.169
to the theology we described above, which
the Foundation labeled SCP-2456-1.

00:07:20.169 --> 00:07:26.919
Those affected by SCP-2456 show an affinity
towards astrology, astronomy, and pseudoscience

00:07:26.919 --> 00:07:31.449
in general, as well as an increased proficiency
in speaking foreign languages.

00:07:31.449 --> 00:07:38.020
There’s also prolonged episodes of psychosis,
paranoia, and Dissociative Identity Disorder,

00:07:38.020 --> 00:07:43.800
as well as a high attention span for geometrical
shapes, patterns, and sequences involving,

00:07:43.800 --> 00:07:46.389
you guessed it, the number five.

00:07:46.389 --> 00:07:51.629
Usually, the SCP-2456 parasite will remain
dormant for a period of time, but once activated

00:07:51.629 --> 00:07:57.419
by several stress triggers, the subject afflicted
with the anomaly will undergo a mind-altering

00:07:57.419 --> 00:08:02.669
revelation, falling asleep for a period of
three to four days, experiencing vivid, cryptic

00:08:02.669 --> 00:08:07.970
dreams involving religious prophets and figures
from various theologies being executed one

00:08:07.970 --> 00:08:13.199
by one with a sword, and celestial bodies
“dancing” in the sky.

00:08:13.199 --> 00:08:18.259
After this long rest, the subject will begin
preaching the -1 religion to others, causing

00:08:18.259 --> 00:08:22.970
the parasite to transmit from one person to
another, bringing more and more followers

00:08:22.970 --> 00:08:24.330
to its cause.

00:08:24.330 --> 00:08:27.110
And after that, the cycle will repeat.

00:08:27.110 --> 00:08:33.480
More followers are attracted, more begin preaching,
and before you can realize, SCP-2456 has affected

00:08:33.480 --> 00:08:35.630
a large group of the Foundation.

00:08:35.630 --> 00:08:39.660
With such an easily transmissible anomaly,
it's a wonder the world hadn’t been taken

00:08:39.660 --> 00:08:46.090
over by SCP-2456 a long time ago, but when
you consider that Fifthism is already an established

00:08:46.090 --> 00:08:50.670
belief system, maybe, in a way, it already
has.

00:08:50.670 --> 00:08:55.910
Believers in the religion that those affected
by SCP-2456 preach are incredibly violent

00:08:55.910 --> 00:09:00.960
and aggressive, with their strong feelings
growing more and more with every new iteration

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:03.000
of the religion over time.

00:09:03.000 --> 00:09:08.050
Believers usually seek out those who haven’t
been affected by SCP-2456, and attempt to

00:09:08.050 --> 00:09:11.300
spread the religion, and if they refuse, murder
them.

00:09:11.300 --> 00:09:15.530
But the Foundation’s research has shown
that no individual that has been affected

00:09:15.530 --> 00:09:23.050
by SCP-2456 has ever been successful in infecting
more than 5% of the existing human population.

00:09:23.050 --> 00:09:28.650
Chalk it up to luck, because Foundation simulations
have indicated that a CK-Class End of the

00:09:28.650 --> 00:09:34.630
World scenario would occur if SCP-2456 infection
rates ever exceed over 7%.

00:09:34.630 --> 00:09:37.500
If you can’t tell, that’s pretty bad.

00:09:37.500 --> 00:09:42.120
Not only that, but the Foundation discovered
that as the religion evolves over time, it

00:09:42.120 --> 00:09:47.050
creates a minor reality-warping effect, and
if left unchecked, can fracture the integrity

00:09:47.050 --> 00:09:49.770
of space and time at a high enough level.

00:09:49.770 --> 00:09:54.560
Thankfully, the Foundation has one way to
combat SCP-2456.

00:09:54.560 --> 00:09:58.960
During the period of time directly after an
individual wakes up from their prophetic sleep,

00:09:58.960 --> 00:10:03.210
treating them with high-class amnestics has
been discovered to completely rid the individual

00:10:03.210 --> 00:10:08.690
of the SCP-2456 parasite, bringing them back
to their senses.

00:10:08.690 --> 00:10:14.090
But still, due to the memetic nature and the
high number of suspected infected individuals,

00:10:14.090 --> 00:10:20.360
the Foundation has found that complete containment
of SCP-2456 is not physically possible, at

00:10:20.360 --> 00:10:23.380
least with the organization’s current technology
level.

00:10:23.380 --> 00:10:28.220
Still, that isn’t stopping researchers from
working tirelessly, trying to develop methods

00:10:28.220 --> 00:10:33.710
of neutralizing all instances of the parasite
in the wild, taking the fight to the internet,

00:10:33.710 --> 00:10:39.470
and making sure that their web-crawlers can
quickly scan for keywords related to SCP-2456

00:10:39.470 --> 00:10:41.910
on websites and social media databases.

00:10:41.910 --> 00:10:47.200
If they’re found, the Foundation can quickly
trace posts to whoever wrote them, and bring

00:10:47.200 --> 00:10:49.950
them to a secure facility for further research.

00:10:49.950 --> 00:10:55.110
It’s never clean work having to abduct civilians
from their homes, but in this case, given

00:10:55.110 --> 00:11:01.060
how dangerous SCP-2456 can be if left unchecked,
it might be justified.

00:11:01.060 --> 00:11:09.450
But how has the religion that SCP-2456 instills
in its victims, SCP-2456-1, evolved over the

00:11:09.450 --> 00:11:10.450
years?

00:11:10.450 --> 00:11:15.020
The manuscripts that the Foundation uncovered
inside the Serpent’s Hand hideaway detailed

00:11:15.020 --> 00:11:17.870
six variations of the theology over time.

00:11:17.870 --> 00:11:19.460
Let’s take a look at them.

00:11:19.460 --> 00:11:23.320
The first variation dates all the way back
to 1837.

00:11:23.320 --> 00:11:29.130
A religion by the name of the “God Worshiping
Society”, which was a fusion of Confucianism

00:11:29.130 --> 00:11:34.990
and Catholicism that cropped up in China at
the time, spread by Hong Xiuquan, a Chinese

00:11:34.990 --> 00:11:39.750
revolutionary who led the Taiping army in
rebellion against the Qing dynasty.

00:11:39.750 --> 00:11:45.830
The stress of having to deal with the political
instability of the era resulted in SCP-2456

00:11:45.830 --> 00:11:51.331
triggering inside Xiuquan’s mind, and causing
him to preach his variation of the -1 religion

00:11:51.331 --> 00:11:52.800
to his followers.

00:11:52.800 --> 00:11:56.820
This furthered the strength of the Taiping
army, allowing them to march through nearly

00:11:56.820 --> 00:12:01.490
every province of China in retaliation until
they achieved their goal.

00:12:01.490 --> 00:12:06.070
Some accounts of Xiuquan’s followers recount
them transforming into piles of geological

00:12:06.070 --> 00:12:11.210
matter, which the Foundation found DNA evidence
bonded to sediment in pockets of igneous rock

00:12:11.210 --> 00:12:12.310
in the area.

00:12:12.310 --> 00:12:17.380
Undoubtedly a result of SCP-2456’s reality
warping side-effects.

00:12:17.380 --> 00:12:23.010
The second variation was found in ancient
Egypt, under the name of the Cult of Aten.

00:12:23.010 --> 00:12:28.420
The progenitor of this variation is unknown,
due to how far back it dates, but the person

00:12:28.420 --> 00:12:34.980
who imposed the will of the Cult of Aten the
most was the then-Pharaoh, Akhenaten of Amarna,

00:12:34.980 --> 00:12:40.570
who used his power as head of state to condemn
worship of all Egyptian deities other than

00:12:40.570 --> 00:12:41.570
Aten.

00:12:41.570 --> 00:12:46.360
The Cult of Aten’s reign over Egypt resulted
in several reality altering properties, including

00:12:46.360 --> 00:12:52.520
strange behavior of celestial bodies, feelings
of stretched out, unending days, and the refusal

00:12:52.520 --> 00:12:58.540
of the sun to set for five days, which resulted
in a drought along the bank of the nile.

00:12:58.540 --> 00:13:03.670
Egyptian star charts from this time display
star systems, constellations, and nebulae

00:13:03.670 --> 00:13:07.170
that do not exist, or are depicted incorrectly.

00:13:07.170 --> 00:13:11.730
The most prominent of these changes include
the inclusion of a planet named “Nbu”,

00:13:11.730 --> 00:13:16.580
which is described as half of the size of
Venus, that would pulsate with light in five

00:13:16.580 --> 00:13:17.580
second intervals.

00:13:17.580 --> 00:13:19.700
There’s that number again.

00:13:19.700 --> 00:13:24.260
The third variation jumps to the time of the
Aztecs, and while little is known about its

00:13:24.260 --> 00:13:28.400
origins, its impact on Aztec society was enormous.

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:33.690
The Aztec deity Tonatiuh was said to be the
fifth sun that set in the sky.

00:13:33.690 --> 00:13:39.220
The Aztecs frequently made sacrifices to Tonatiuh,
and the worship of the entity caused a reality

00:13:39.220 --> 00:13:41.420
warping effect throughout the empire.

00:13:41.420 --> 00:13:47.480
The sun and the moon were eclipsed by unknown
celestial objects consistently for weeks.

00:13:47.480 --> 00:13:52.310
Bodies from past sacrifices would reanimate
and attack civilians, reaching into their

00:13:52.310 --> 00:13:54.650
throats and pulling out their hearts.

00:13:54.650 --> 00:13:59.760
The coasts of the empire suffered from glowing
red poisons, which killed off fish and caused

00:13:59.760 --> 00:14:04.870
tissue necrosis in humans, as well as forming
large blood clots in the lungs.

00:14:04.870 --> 00:14:09.550
The fourth variation, the Cult of the Supreme
Being, was a short-lived religion perpetrated

00:14:09.550 --> 00:14:15.090
by French philosopher Augustin Robespierre
during the time of the French Revolution.

00:14:15.090 --> 00:14:18.970
Its small longevity meant that the religion
didn’t garner enough followers to cause

00:14:18.970 --> 00:14:24.520
intense reality-warping effects, but some
anomalous characteristics were still prevalent,

00:14:24.520 --> 00:14:29.500
such as reports of incorporeal manifestations
in the streets of Paris, dimensional shifts

00:14:29.500 --> 00:14:34.990
in salons and smoking parlors around the city,
and the increased brutality and ruthlessness

00:14:34.990 --> 00:14:40.440
of the revolutionaries, who imposed a large
daily quota of executions.

00:14:40.440 --> 00:14:43.490
The fifth variation is entirely unknown.

00:14:43.490 --> 00:14:47.750
Most likely to do with the number’s significance
to the Fifthist belief system, attempts to

00:14:47.750 --> 00:14:54.920
access the SCP Foundation files on the fifth
incarnation of SCP-2456-1’s belief system

00:14:54.920 --> 00:14:58.320
are met with failure, as the files data is
corrupted.

00:14:58.320 --> 00:15:01.270
This, however, raises a new question.

00:15:01.270 --> 00:15:05.500
Maybe this unknown religion is still one that’s
active today.

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:12.170
Maybe the fifth variation of SCP-2456-1 is
Fifthism itself, having evolved as a variation

00:15:12.170 --> 00:15:15.370
of SCP-2456 over the years.

00:15:15.370 --> 00:15:20.670
That would add a whole new level of danger
to Fifthism, as if it got out of hand, the

00:15:20.670 --> 00:15:26.590
reality warping effects of being a SCP-2456
based theology would cause destruction to

00:15:26.590 --> 00:15:28.710
the fabric of reality itself.

00:15:28.710 --> 00:15:34.320
The sixth variation is similar to the fifth,
with its files being similarly corrupted in

00:15:34.320 --> 00:15:40.440
the Foundation’s databases and all information
on it being entirely unknown, save for a single

00:15:40.440 --> 00:15:46.260
readable sentence which states that the main
perpetrator, the prophet of this sixth variation

00:15:46.260 --> 00:15:53.500
of SCP-2456-1, is still at large today, remaining
a threat to the world.

00:15:53.500 --> 00:15:58.520
Knowing that this virus can affect large swathes
of the population, as it did in the Aztec

00:15:58.520 --> 00:16:05.690
and Egyptian empires, the Foundation remains
extremely cautious of SCP-2456, especially

00:16:05.690 --> 00:16:10.760
with the added risk of Fifthism being prevalent
in the anomalous world, and the unknown sixth

00:16:10.760 --> 00:16:12.980
religion still at large.

00:16:12.980 --> 00:16:16.740
Also discovered inside the Serpent’s Hand
warehouse were several manuscripts from the

00:16:16.740 --> 00:16:20.820
various religions that SCP-2456 influenced.

00:16:20.820 --> 00:16:25.261
Scriptures from the Cult of Aten, letters
written by Robespierre in his journal, and

00:16:25.261 --> 00:16:30.900
even a text from the Taiping revolution, labeled
the Wisdoms of the Heavenly King.

00:16:30.900 --> 00:16:32.830
But what did they say?

00:16:32.830 --> 00:16:37.390
The text sourced from China described the
story of a Prophet, who wanted to bring great

00:16:37.390 --> 00:16:39.780
knowledge to the people beneath him.

00:16:39.780 --> 00:16:45.510
And so, as the text describes, he followed
the smoke, a Fifthist metaphor for reaching

00:16:45.510 --> 00:16:46.510
enlightenment.

00:16:46.510 --> 00:16:52.140
He did so by studying alongside a mentor for
five months, and on the fifth day of the fifth

00:16:52.140 --> 00:16:57.010
month, he had achieved enlightenment, and
knew he had a great mission to complete.

00:16:57.010 --> 00:17:02.730
He roused his subjects, rallying the people
who lived in ash and filth to war, attacking

00:17:02.730 --> 00:17:05.860
with the power of the sun on their side.

00:17:05.860 --> 00:17:10.329
Those who faced the Prophet ran, but the ones
who were left understood.

00:17:10.329 --> 00:17:16.230
On the Fifth day, they turned into tar, sand,
and salt, and the Prophet remained victorious.

00:17:16.230 --> 00:17:17.440
Sound familiar?

00:17:17.440 --> 00:17:21.290
It’s an abridged retelling of Hong Xiuquan’s
revolution.

00:17:21.290 --> 00:17:25.740
The rest of the text describes a parable of
a master and a student philosophizing about

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:29.150
the stars, with a particular poem that stands
out.

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:30.400
It reads:

00:17:30.400 --> 00:17:35.160
Five spokes of a broken star
Five elements that forever spar

00:17:35.160 --> 00:17:40.360
Five senses to evoke the mind
Five pieces slowly unwind.

00:17:40.360 --> 00:17:46.300
A Black Moon, howling, is a vision unworthy
of one's sight.

00:17:46.300 --> 00:17:51.420
A hymn sourced from the Cult of Aten also
makes references to the number five, and specifically

00:17:51.420 --> 00:17:53.330
makes mention of the “Black Moon”.

00:17:53.330 --> 00:17:58.390
If you’re familiar with the SCP Foundation’s
inner circle, the Overseer Council, then you

00:17:58.390 --> 00:18:02.770
know that they frequently use the phrase “Does
the Black Moon Howl?”

00:18:02.770 --> 00:18:06.780
as a security measure to access top-secret,
confidential documents.

00:18:06.780 --> 00:18:10.100
Its true meaning, however, remains shrouded
in mystery.

00:18:10.100 --> 00:18:12.350
But here, you see it connected to SCP-2456.

00:18:12.350 --> 00:18:15.190
It can’t be a coincidence.

00:18:15.190 --> 00:18:19.850
Robespierre’s diary describes an account
of the French revolution, detailing Robespierre’s

00:18:19.850 --> 00:18:25.440
descent into madness that led to the creation
of the short-lived Cult of the Supreme Being.

00:18:25.440 --> 00:18:31.020
The revolution descends into brutality, and
as Robespierre describes, “the streets run

00:18:31.020 --> 00:18:36.360
pink with blood and agony” as the Cult revels
in the bloodshed and ruthlessness.

00:18:36.360 --> 00:18:42.610
All of this points to a compelling mystery
about the true nature of SCP-2456, especially

00:18:42.610 --> 00:18:47.980
with the connection to the commonly used symbol
of the Black Moon in the SCP Foundation.

00:18:47.980 --> 00:18:54.730
And all of this came to a head on December
21st, 2016, when an unidentifiable audio file

00:18:54.730 --> 00:18:58.860
was sent to a Foundation Researcher that alerted
the server's firewalls.

00:18:58.860 --> 00:19:04.150
The audio file was traced as originating from
a cubicle that had been vacant for six years,

00:19:04.150 --> 00:19:07.650
with hardware that had been short-circuited
and badly corroded.

00:19:07.650 --> 00:19:11.720
A portion of the audio file was recovered
from the damaged terminal, and the Foundation

00:19:11.720 --> 00:19:13.550
quickly began to transcribe it.

00:19:13.550 --> 00:19:18.930
It was the voice of an unknown Foundation
employee, who detailed that he had been working

00:19:18.930 --> 00:19:23.370
with the organization for two decades, and
that while he had seen horrible things in

00:19:23.370 --> 00:19:27.890
the past, as he was recording this message,
he was more terrified than ever before.

00:19:27.890 --> 00:19:34.860
He was assigned to research SCP-2456, cataloging
all the past occurrences of the various religions

00:19:34.860 --> 00:19:38.760
that had cropped up as a result of the parasite
over the years.

00:19:38.760 --> 00:19:44.420
He had experience in memetics, but the danger
of researching SCP-2456 was proving difficult

00:19:44.420 --> 00:19:45.970
to contend with.

00:19:45.970 --> 00:19:51.600
Members of the research team were succumbing
to SCP-2456, but not only that, they were

00:19:51.600 --> 00:19:53.280
disappearing too.

00:19:53.280 --> 00:19:57.670
After one personnel was admitted to an infirmary,
the speaker recounted that he was never able

00:19:57.670 --> 00:19:59.480
to find them again.

00:19:59.480 --> 00:20:05.930
The audio continued to play, and the speaker
explained that SCP-2456 also carries a potent

00:20:05.930 --> 00:20:12.090
anti-meme, an idea that causes dramatic reality
shifts, often characterized by something being

00:20:12.090 --> 00:20:15.990
imperceptible and unrecognizable to the human
brain.

00:20:15.990 --> 00:20:21.950
Whenever information about a SCP-2456 religion
is read or written about, the anti-meme will

00:20:21.950 --> 00:20:27.360
enter the subject and slowly erase them from
existence, alongside all records and knowledge

00:20:27.360 --> 00:20:28.360
of the subject.

00:20:28.360 --> 00:20:31.470
Sometimes, however, corpses and names remain.

00:20:31.470 --> 00:20:35.460
The speaker detailed how he witnessed his
peers slowly disappear.

00:20:35.460 --> 00:20:39.480
As the file goes on, he descends into typical
fifthist ranting.

00:20:39.480 --> 00:20:45.720
Speaking about fives, following the smoke,
and a dream, but he leaves a terrifying message:

00:20:45.720 --> 00:20:49.160
The Foundation is old, but the world is older.

00:20:49.160 --> 00:20:54.720
Maybe the Serpent’s Hand, with their manuscripts
and research on SCP-2456 were attempting to

00:20:54.720 --> 00:21:00.020
keep the forces of the Fifth King, a mysterious
deity the man mentions, at bay.

00:21:00.020 --> 00:21:05.260
Now, inside the hands of the Foundation, these
documents will never be destroyed.

00:21:05.260 --> 00:21:09.650
They will continue to be read, and continue
to linger in reality.

00:21:09.650 --> 00:21:14.240
The speaker signs off, ranting more about
the Star Signals incident, and the Fifthist

00:21:14.240 --> 00:21:17.510
Dream that permeates the shadows of all reality.

00:21:17.510 --> 00:21:22.790
As the speaker states, “Once history is
forgotten, it is of course doomed to repeat

00:21:22.790 --> 00:21:23.790
itself.

00:21:23.790 --> 00:21:27.260
And the sixth cycle will forever more echo.”

00:21:27.260 --> 00:21:33.910
Now go check out “SCP-001 - The Broken God
- Ouroboros Cycle” and “Children of SCP-001

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:40.120
The Scarlet King - Is SCP-999 Really His Son?”
for more anomalous religions and their bizarre

00:21:40.120 --> 00:21:42.250
followers from SCP Explained!

